From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: h713: bind the AV1 decoder to hantro

Move the AV1 node from the presence probe's compatible to the decoder's,
and name the video engine whose module clock, bus clock and reset the
core runs from, so the driver can link to it.

Adapted for this series from the original: the original's hunk changes
the node its 0140 added for the AV1 presence probe (compatible
"allwinner,sun50i-h713-av1-probe"). This series has neither 0140 nor the
probe (0141), so the hunk adds the node whole -- 0140's node and comment
with the original's change applied, which is the node the original
series ends with, in the same place (after the video engine). The node
the board patch 0024 already carries at this address
(av1-decoder@1c0d000, "allwinner,sunxi-google-ve", resets RST_BUS_VE and
RST_BUS_VE3) stays, as it does in the original series: no driver binds
it, so it claims none of its clocks or resets.

Origin: https://github.com/cstenger/allwinner-h713-mainline/blob/43b2cdd4aa1b161a281db8b10f02ce70085e2d42/patches/kernel/0146-arm64-dts-h713-bind-the-av1-decoder-to-hantro.patch (0146-arm64-dts-h713-bind-the-av1-decoder-to-hantro.patch, commit 46bc559, adapted; with 0140-arm64-dts-h713-add-the-av1-decoder-node.patch, commit 3ca3a5e)
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -1462,6 +1462,56 @@
 			status = "okay";
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * The AV1 decoder -- Google IP, not Allwinner's and not
+		 * VeriSilicon's. The stock DTB calls it
+		 * compatible = "allwinner,sunxi-google-ve" at this address, and
+		 * libawav1.so is built around taffel::ctypes::SwRegisters and
+		 * BigSeaRegisters, which are Google AV1 codenames. There is no
+		 * driver for it in any tree; mainline's only AV1 backend is
+		 * Rockchip's VPU981, whose register file reaches 394 where this
+		 * block's holds 292. See
+		 * docs/reference/vp9-av1-codec-scouting-2026-09-24.md.
+		 *
+		 * This node exists so a probe driver can read the core ID and
+		 * settle two questions at once: whether the block is alive on
+		 * this die, and which of its two register-file variants this is
+		 * (AsicRegisterMapWidth picks 1168 or 816 bytes by comparing an
+		 * ID against 0xb16c).
+		 *
+		 * DELIBERATELY NARROWER THAN STOCK. The vendor node also lists
+		 * "bus_ve" and "reset_ve", and both are cedrus's. A reset is not
+		 * safely shared: deasserting reset_ve here could reset the video
+		 * engine underneath a running decode. bus_av1 and mbus_av1 are
+		 * this block's own, and reset_av1 has no other consumer, so the
+		 * probe takes only those. If the ID reads as garbage, adding
+		 * bus_ve as a SHARED CLOCK (refcounted, unlike a reset) is the
+		 * next thing to try -- not reset_ve.
+		 *
+		 * The "av1" module clock the stock node lists is absent from our
+		 * CCU and is deliberately not required here: it drives the
+		 * decode core, while register access needs only the bus clock.
+		 */
+		av1: av1@1c0d000 {
+			/*
+			 * Decoded by hantro's H713 variant. The core also runs
+			 * from the VE's module clock and needs the VE's bus
+			 * clock and reset released; those stay cedrus's, and
+			 * the driver keeps them up through a runtime-PM link
+			 * to the VE named here.
+			 */
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h713-av1";
+			reg = <0x01c0d000 0x1000>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 107 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_AV1>, <&ccu CLK_MBUS_AV1>;
+			clock-names = "bus", "mbus";
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_AV1>;
+			allwinner,video-engine = <&ve>;
+			iommus = <&iommu 5 1>;
+			power-domains = <&ppu 4>;
+			status = "okay";
+		};
+
 		/* === GPU (Mali-G31 Bifrost, Panfrost driver) === */
 		gpu: gpu@1800000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h616-mali",
